  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-independent-bnpl-preset-container (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific binary payload from Cloudflare Workers C2 endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS fails, it falls back to a DNS TXT chunked transfer channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru / net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched detached (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u0026amp;\" on Unix), executing attacker-controlled code on the host.",
  "affected": [
    {
      "package": {
        "ecosystem": "npm",
